From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Neil Johnson <189873278+Zesty0wl@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] agent: Accept clipboard releases with no data

VDAgentClipboardRelease has no fields, so clients such as QEMU send
releases without any data. Compilers that don't allow empty structures,
such as MSVC, give it a size, so the agent rejected every release as the
wrong size and stopped, and clipboard changes made in the guest while it
restarted were lost.
---
 common/agent.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/common/agent.c b/common/agent.c
index e7df786..3639106 100644
--- a/common/agent.c
+++ b/common/agent.c
@@ -54,7 +54,9 @@ static const int agent_message_min_size[] =
     sizeof(VDAgentAnnounceCapabilities), /* VD_AGENT_ANNOUNCE_CAPABILITIES */
     sizeof(VDAgentClipboardGrab), /* VD_AGENT_CLIPBOARD_GRAB */
     sizeof(VDAgentClipboardRequest), /* VD_AGENT_CLIPBOARD_REQUEST */
-    sizeof(VDAgentClipboardRelease), /* VD_AGENT_CLIPBOARD_RELEASE */
+    /* VDAgentClipboardRelease has no fields, but compilers that don't allow empty structures, such as MSVC,
+     * give it a size, which would make the agent reject every release that a client sends. */
+    0, /* VD_AGENT_CLIPBOARD_RELEASE */
     sizeof(VDAgentFileXferStartMessage), /* VD_AGENT_FILE_XFER_START */
     sizeof(VDAgentFileXferStatusMessage), /* VD_AGENT_FILE_XFER_STATUS */
     sizeof(VDAgentFileXferDataMessage), /* VD_AGENT_FILE_XFER_DATA */
